# Notice on the processing of personal data — EU {{ project.name }} Project

**Version {{ doc.version }}**

{% call text.wrap() %}{{ platform.short }} is committed to protecting the personal data entrusted to it. Their management and security are therefore ensured with the utmost care, as required by data protection law (Regulation (EU) 2016/679 - GDPR and Italian Legislative Decree 196/2003).{% endcall %}

This notice explains who we are, for which purposes we use your data, how we manage it,
to whom it is disclosed and what your rights are.

## 1. Who will process my data?

{% call text.wrap() %}Your data will be processed by {{ platform.name }} in {{ platform.country.en }}, with registered office at {{ platform.registered_office }}.{% endcall %}

{% call text.wrap() %}For more information, you can contact the company at: {{ platform.pec }}.{% endcall %}

{% call text.wrap() %}{{ text.poss(platform.short) }} Data Protection Officer, appointed by the controller, can be contacted by email at: {{ platform.dpo }}.{% endcall %}

## 2. Which data will be processed?

- identification and contact data (name, tax code, email, phone, address);
- point of delivery (POD) and supply address;
{% if features.document_extraction %}
- copies of an electricity bill;
{% endif %}
- energy data from meters and devices, and data derived from it (forecasts, suggestions,
  commitments, points).

## 3. Why do you need my data?

{{ platform.short }} will use your data solely for the following purpose:

- the {{ project.name }} research project, Grant Agreement No. {{ project.grant_agreement }}.

We will not process data beyond what the purposes pursued require, and we will not use
your data for purposes other than those described in this notice.

## 4. How will you use my data?

{% call text.wrap() %}{{ platform.short }} aims to protect the personal data entrusted to it, processing it in accordance with the principles of fairness, lawfulness and transparency.{% endcall %}

Your data will therefore be processed with tools and procedures suitable for ensuring
the utmost security and confidentiality, in archives, with the help of digital media and
computer and telematic means.

## 5. How long will you keep my data?

{% call text.wrap() %}The data collected will be kept for as long as needed for the purposes above, and in any case no later than the end of the project, scheduled for {{ text.date(project.end, 'en') }}. At the end of that period, all personal data processed will be deleted.{% endcall %}

## 6. Will you share my information with others?

{% call text.wrap() %}Following the collection of the data by {{ platform.short }}, the personal data relating to this processing will not be disclosed to third parties.{% endcall %}

## 7. What are my rights?

With regard to the data processed by the controller, you may exercise the following
rights:

- to be informed of the processing of your personal data and, where applicable, to
  receive a copy of it: the data subject's right of access (Art. 15 of the EU
  Regulation);
- to have inaccurate personal data concerning you corrected: the right to rectification
  (Art. 16 of the EU Regulation);
- to have your personal data erased without undue delay: the right to be forgotten
  (Art. 17 of the EU Regulation);
- to restrict the processing of your personal data. Where certain conditions apply, you
  may ask for the processing of your data to be restricted; the controller will then not
  process the data for any purpose other than storing it (Art. 18 of the EU Regulation);
- to receive your data, or have it transmitted to another controller (Art. 20 of the EU
  Regulation);
- to object to the processing of your data. You may object to the processing of your
  data where it is based on a legal basis other than consent (Art. 21 of the EU
  Regulation);
- not to be subject to automated decision-making (Art. 22 of the EU Regulation).

Further information on the data subject's rights is available at
www.garanteprivacy.it.

These rights can be exercised as provided by the Regulation:

{% call text.wrap('- ') %}by email to {{ platform.pec }} or {{ platform.dpo }};{% endcall %}
{% call text.wrap('- ') %}by registered letter with return receipt to the controller's registered office at {{ platform.registered_office }}.{% endcall %}

Under Art. 7 of the EU Regulation, withdrawing consent does not affect the lawfulness of
processing based on consent before its withdrawal. A data subject who believes their
rights have been infringed has the right to lodge a complaint with the Italian Data
Protection Authority (Garante per la protezione dei dati personali), as the Authority
indicates at www.garanteprivacy.it.

## 8. Automated decision-making

{% call text.wrap() %}{{ platform.short }} does not carry out any processing of personal data that consists of automated decision-making.{% endcall %}

## 9. Legal basis

The legal basis of the processing above is:

{% call text.wrap('- ') %}Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR: the data subject has consented to the processing of their personal data for the specific purpose, through the online data collection page.{% endcall %}
